- Spousal support amount, duration, and enforcement method
- Child custody/visitation schedule, child support calculation method, health insurance and childcare provisions
- QDRO and tax allocation language for retirement accounts
- Requirement for life insurance or wage assignment to secure support (if applicable)
- Attorney fees and costs allocation
- Confidentiality/non-disparagement if appropriate (weigh against immigration transparency)
- Enforcement clauses and jurisdiction (which court will enforce)
- Language confirming the settlement isn’t an admission for immigration purposes (ask attorney about wording)

5) Short checklist for the immediate next meeting/hearing
- Bring the documents listed above (especially immigration notices and financials).
- Tell Amy exactly what changed about your immigration status and provide copies.
- Ask Amy if she recommends an immigration attorney and if she will coordinate with them.
- Identify any safety concerns that might require a protective order.
- Get clarity on costs and a written plan for the next 60–90 days (milestones and responsibilities).
- Decide whether to propose mediation or direct settlement negotiations, and ask about timing relative to the immigration hearing.

