I can help — below is a focused checklist and set of questions to take to Amy Foster (and to any immigration counsel) so you’re prepared for settlement talks and the next legal steps. I’ve organized it by priority and topic so you can pick what’s most important.

Immediate priorities (ask these first)
- Do I have automatic protections now? (E.g., California automatic restraining orders on disposing of community property, cancelling insurance, or removing children.)
- What immediate temporary orders should we request now (spousal support, child support, custody/visitation, exclusive use of the home, restraining orders)?
- Given my status change, should we pause any settlement negotiations until we confirm immigration implications?

Immigration-specific questions
- How does my change in immigration status affect the divorce and settlement options available to me?
- Could any settlement term (e.g., waiving alimony, signing releases, admitting anything about our marriage) harm my immigration case or any pending immigration applications or relief?
- Are there immigration remedies I should consider now (adjustment of status, VAWA, U-visa, cancellation of removal, deferred action)? If you’re not immigration counsel, can you refer or coordinate with an immigration attorney?
- If my ex-spouse is/was a sponsor or filed immigration paperwork (I-130, affidavit of support), what happens to those filings if we divorce or settle?
- Can settlement include a clause requiring my ex to cooperate in immigration paperwork (e.g., signing affidavits)? Is that enforceable and safe?
- Will anything we agree to in family court or in writing be discoverable or usable in immigration court?

Financial & property division (California/community property focus)
- Under California law, how will our assets and debts likely be divided? What counts as community property vs. separate property here?
- How are retirement accounts, 401(k), pensions, stock options, business ownership, and tax refunds handled in a settlement?
- How will debts (credit cards, mortgage, business debts) be allocated — and how do we ensure my credit is protected (removal from joint accounts, refinances)?
- Should we ask for an escrow/holdback for disputed assets or tax liabilities?
- How are tax consequences handled (capital gains, transfer of property, alimony vs. taxable?).

Support, custody & family matters
- If children are involved: custody, visitation, child support guidelines, parental relocation restrictions, and who pays for childcare/education/medical.
- Health insurance: how do I keep coverage? Will COBRA apply or can spousal support cover health premiums?
