Priority framing (decide before the meeting)
- What outcome matters most to you? (e.g., stay in U.S., custody time, cash now vs. long-term support, keep the house, protect retirement)
- Which issues are non-negotiable and which can be traded in negotiation?

Questions to ask your attorney — settlement terms and strategy
- Should we negotiate a settlement now or delay because of the immigration proceedings? What are the risks/benefits of settling early?
- What overall negotiation strategy do you recommend (mediation, private settlement, court-ordered settlement conference)?
- How much settlement authority will you have? Do I need to sign any authorization giving you final say?
- What would be a reasonable opening demand and realistic bottom line for me?

Financial & property division
- How will community vs. separate property be treated in California here? Are there assets that need forensic accounting?
- What documents do you need from me to evaluate asset division (bank accounts, retirement, deeds, business valuations)?
- How should joint debts be allocated and secured (who pays, lien releases, co-signed debt)?
