Our first hearing is next month and I want to be prepared for settlement discussions. Below are topics and questions I’d like to cover at our next meeting (or phone call). Please advise which items you want me to bring and whether you recommend seeking any immediate temporary orders.

- Immigration: how divorce/settlement terms could affect my current immigration case; language to avoid; possible relief options (VAWA, adjustment, other)
- Temporary orders: custody, support, exclusive use of home, asset preservation, protective orders
- Finances: preservation of assets, temporary spousal/child support, valuation of assets and debts, tax consequences
- Custody: temporary parenting plan, support, travel/relocation issues, implications for children’s immigration
- Settlement strategy: mediation vs negotiation, confidentiality, settlement authority, enforcement provisions
- Evidence & discovery: specific documents to gather now
- Costs and timeline: expected costs to trial vs settlement; how settlement offers will be communicated to me

Documents I can bring: passport/immigration docs, marriage certificate, bank/credit statements, pay stubs, tax returns, titles/deeds, communications related to the case. Tell me if you need anything else.

Can we schedule a meeting or call this week to go over strategy?

Thanks,
[Your name]

