  - How will we handle legal fees — do we seek the other party to pay fees or include a fee-shifting clause if they breach?
  - How do we structure enforceability and remedies for breaches (attorney-fee shifting, contempt, liens)?
- Paperwork, timeline, and next steps
  - What filings will you make before the first hearing and what do I need to prepare?
  - What’s our trial timeline and discovery schedule?
  - What should I say or not say to the other party or on social media while this is ongoing?
- Confidentiality & releases
  - What confidentiality/privacy language should be in the settlement to protect me (non-disparagement, sealed filings, limits on disclosure of immigration info)?
  - Will signing a settlement require me to make admissions that could affect immigration?
- Practical & tax considerations
  - Tax consequences of division (who pays taxes on investment gains, alimony tax treatment if relevant)?
  - How are retirement accounts/pensions divided and what paperwork (QDRO) is needed?
- Communication with you
  - How will you keep me updated and how quickly can I reach you with urgent questions?
  - Do we need to coordinate with any other counsel (immigration, tax, business valuation)?

Documents to bring / collect (bring originals if possible)
- IDs, passports, green card, visa, I-94, USCIS/EOIR receipts, immigration court documents
- Marriage certificate, any pre/post-nups, separation agreements
- Recent pay stubs, tax returns (3 years), W-2s, 1099s, benefit statements
